From: relay12 contributors
Subject: [PATCH] dtl: provide the missing unsigned SIZET-safe helpers

llvm-mingw's <intsafe.h> declares SSIZETAdd/SSIZETMult (the signed
variants) but not SIZETAdd/SIZETMult, which FormatDescImpl.cpp uses for
overflow-checked SIZE_T arithmetic exactly as Microsoft's own intsafe.h
intends. Microsoft's header declares both families; this MinGW header
ships only one, so these calls are undeclared identifiers under this
toolchain.

compat/relay_intsafe_compat.hpp supplies the two missing functions,
included after <intsafe.h> so it can rely on that header's own
INTSAFE_E_ARITHMETIC_OVERFLOW without redefining it. Not guarded against
a future toolchain adding these: a redefinition error at that point is a
clearer signal than a speculative guard, and is exactly when this patch
should be deleted.
---
diff --git a/src/FormatDescImpl.cpp b/src/FormatDescImpl.cpp
index 69565e3..eb096ca 100644
--- a/src/FormatDescImpl.cpp
+++ b/src/FormatDescImpl.cpp
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 // Licensed under the MIT License.
 #include <pch.h>
 #include <intsafe.h>
+#include "relay_intsafe_compat.hpp"
 
 #define R D3D11FCN_R
 #define G D3D11FCN_G
